# Shared Header (mandatory)

Every user-facing page **must** use the shared `Header` from `components/header.tsx`, rendered once in `app/layout.tsx`. This is not optional.

## Required pattern

- Add new pages as `app/**/page.tsx` routes so they inherit `app/layout.tsx` automatically.
- Page components render **only** their main content (`<main>` or equivalent). Never add `<header class="site-header">`, inline nav links, or duplicate burger menus.
- Register canonical URLs in `lib/nav.ts` and `lib/static-page-routes.ts` (no `/pages/*.html` links in app code).

## Forbidden

- Duplicating header/nav markup in HTML or TSX page files
- Creating standalone `.html` pages with their own navigation (legacy `pages/*.html` are redirect stubs only)
- Loading `site-header.css` / `site-nav.js` inside page content — layout owns header styles and behaviour

## Migrating legacy static pages

1. Extract body content (hero + main) into `components/static-pages/*-content.static.tsx` (see `scripts/html-to-static-tsx.mjs`)
2. Add `app/<route>/page.tsx` that imports the content component
3. Add a redirect in `lib/static-page-routes.ts`
4. Run `node scripts/stub-legacy-html.mjs` to replace the old HTML file with a redirect stub

## If you see a page without the shared Header

Treat it as a **bug** and fix immediately by migrating to an App Router page or removing duplicate header markup.
